WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.100
"Begin a new quest?"

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.730
"Begin a new quest?"
"Yes" "No"

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.400
Let's get to our schoolwork.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.990
Starting with whoever's ready:

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.450
Come and get me!

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:33.550
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:42.980
"Nagisa"

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:44.640
"Karma"

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:45.640
"Kaede"

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:46.980
"Isogai" "Maehara"

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.650
"Rio" "Okuda" "Sugino" "Kanzaki"

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.150
"Chiba" "Hayami"

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:52.650
"Hinata" "Meg"

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:55.150
"Hinano" "Takebayashi" "Toka" "Justice"

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:57.160
"Muramatsu" "Kirara" "Yoshida" "Terasaka"

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.160
"Okajima" "Hara" "Mimura" "Fuwa" "Sugaya"

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.160
"Karasuma" "Irina"

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:17.470
"The E Class and the Big Bad"

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.890
You've got a long way to go
before you're heroes, class.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:21.310
"The E Class did their best"

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.350
--That's the way!
--Our attacks don't connect!

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:23.350
"A miss! No damage hath been scored!"

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:24.810
Whoops! I got away!

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.560
"A miss!"

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.520
He's too fast!

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.520
"The Big Bad is smiling"

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.940
Like we can beat the Big Bad!

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.950
We're still level 1!

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.780
With just Cypress Sticks for equipment.

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:35.740
Heck, mine's plastic!

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.950
You're the mightiest!

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.700
"That's for unclogging toilets!"

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.700
Not that! It's way too filthy!

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.410
Even Isogai. At first glance,
he's got a wicked suit of armor...

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.040
...but he's only wearing the front half.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.670
That's his butt!

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.670
We're poor--I could only afford half.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.250
Do they even <i>sell</i> them like that?!

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.220
In any case, we're nowhere near ready.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.660
Besides, why us? Why the misfit E Class?

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.850
Kunugigaoka School of Magic,

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:08.700
where they teach students how to be heroes.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:12.100
And a satellite campus for misfits,
hidden on the back of the mountain.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.780
That's where the E Class alone

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:18.080
shared a special secret
the other classes didn't know:

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:23.160
For some reason, the 
teacher instructing us...

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.370
...was the Big Bad!

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.330
Oh! So he really <i>does</i> exist!

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.830
Koro-Q!

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:30.330
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.790
"Some days ago"

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:37.420
"Royal Knight Commander" "Karasuma"

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:37.420
Let me be blunt: I want 
you to kill this fellow.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:44.140
How do you do? I'm the Big Bad,
and as of today, I'm your teacher.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:45.850
Yeah, I don't think so.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.690
Even as Big Bads go, he's extremely fast.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:51.440
Big Bads are fast?!

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.810
We could never pull it off!

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.520
Why us?

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:58.750
There's only one way
to land attacks on this guy,

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.820
and that's via your buggy abilities.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:02.490
Huh?

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.280
You're no misfits.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.540
In fact, each and every one of you
is a special individual.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.040
For example, Isogai:

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.250
Your being able to buy only
the front half of a suit of armor is a bug.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:16.460
What? It's not because I'm poor?!

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:21.300
Rich or poor, no one can buy
only the front half of a suit of armor.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.600
So me only being able 
to equip bathroom tools?

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.180
And how my magic attracts insects?

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:27.970
Bugs.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.770
And my small chest?

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:31.940
And how I can't throw away
the dirty mags I find?

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:33.810
"Smut"

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.810
Unfortunately, those are <i>not</i> bugs!

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.020
A Big Bad impervious to any attack:

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:39.360
We need people like you to defeat him.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.690
Oh...

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.160
So I made your government an offer:

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:47.870
I'll train up the E Class to a point
where you <i>can</i> defeat me.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:48.950
Why?!

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.160
Overwhelming strength...

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.080
No one has ever felt quite this lonesome.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.880
I'm anxious for someone to appear
whom I may fight on an equal footing.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.210
In short...

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:01.840
"Bad"

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.840
I wanna fight someone stronger!

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.090
And now you know.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.010
He's really into it...

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.300
Mr.--er, Commander Karasuma!

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.430
Hmm?

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.850
Do we have any limits or anything?

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.140
What do you mean?

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.020
Ah, so it depends on our popularity.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.860
An unkillable Big Bad for a teacher:

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:18.650
We decided on...

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.400
Koro Sensei!

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.240
...for his name.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.700
And so Koro Sensei and the E Class

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.120
were about to embark on
one truly unusual adventure.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.240
Koro-Q!

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.580
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.040
"Ace Sorceress: Confessing the Truth"

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.790
Say it! Come on! Spill your secret!

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:40.130
If you want a little brother or sister,
go to sleep already!

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:42.720
Whaaat?!

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.680
Koro-Q!

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.090
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.850
"Tell Us, Mr. Principal!"

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.660
Tell Us, Mr. Principal!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:54.440
Hello, students. Principal Gakuho Asano here.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:59.360
Seems we have a lot of questions
from distressed students again today.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.820
Now, let's try to address their concerns.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:08.130
Here's one from "Longing for a 2D Life":

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:11.950
"I study with all my might every day,

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.580
but I'm just not seeing any results.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.040
Please teach me a good way to study."

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:18.850
Hmm.

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:21.250
Takebayashi...

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.970
You don't even know
the criteria for "all your might."

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:31.760
You're saying you forego sleep,
meals, excretory functions?

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:35.350
When you're coughing up blood
and sense Death's approach,

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.490
<i>then</i> you can say "with all my might."

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:41.110
And besides, if you have the time
to send in this question,

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:42.570
aren't there other things you ought to be--

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:43.890
Koro-Q!

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:44.570
"Koro Sensei Quest"

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.780
"Level 1: Plains"

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:49.030
Today I'll have you
defeat your archenemy, the slime.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.120
Slimes are our archenemies, huh?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.040
We<i> are</i> pretty weak.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.450
"We can't even defeat a slime."

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.710
If you can only release yourself
from that mindset, break that spell,

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:02.000
you're sure to advance as warriors.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.920
Seems the slimes around here
are on the hunt--and full of themselves.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:09.220
Let's teach them a lesson.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.430
Oh! Look!

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:11.680
Hey, hey, hey!

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:14.060
Quit acting all big, E Class!

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:17.430
Who said you could come onto our turf?

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.270
"Some Slime Kunudons draw near!"

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.440
They're<i> way</i> full of themselves...

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.020
Huh?

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.480
What? That's the Big Bad!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.570
What's he doing in this starting area?

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:25.360
I know!

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:29.070
He's here to sacrifice those humans
with his own hands!

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.280
If it isn't the Big Bad!

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.120
How nice of you to visit such a dull place.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.540
It's not much, but please...

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:41.170
Now, let's get down to 
sacrificing these slimes.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.000
Wait--

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.670
You're sacrificing...<i> us</i>?!

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:59.120
I'm the one you want!

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:00.020
What a man!

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.290
But his butt is showing!

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:02.210
Stand back, everyone!

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:03.750
Still: what a man!

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:04.900
<i>How</i>?!

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.120
Okay, then I'll just...

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.230
Disgusting!

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.360
<i>Why</i>?!

00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:12.820
"The Slime Kunudons called for help!"

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.290
Koro Sensei, I'll give it a try!

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:20.750
That's some nice bloodlust.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.790
We'd been called misfits and just given up.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.550
Now, for the first time,
it felt like we were thinking positive.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:29.550
If we do our best here... we can change!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.530
Nagisa?!

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:36.510
What happened?!

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:40.980
It would appear Nagisa's bug
is randomized every time.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:45.940
With this weird bug, if I can just
hit them like I mean it, I--

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.940
"Status" "STR 99999"

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:46.940
I can do it!

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.400
Fire!

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:58.580
Yesss! I beat my first slime!

00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:00.290
"Nagisa's level increases!"

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.290
What, with <i>magic</i>?!

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.580
Now that Nagisa's shown us
how it's done, we have to step up, too!

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.000
We'll show 'em the
combined power of the E Class!

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.420
Hey! Ow! Wait!

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.770
Who do you think you are?!

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.300
Just kidding! Forgive us!

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.580
Should we lick your boots?

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:14.930
Argh! Lickity lick-lick-lick...

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:18.150
We're done with you for today!

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:22.270
"The E Class's level increases!"

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:28.440
Excellent! Seems that
"misfit mindset" spell has been broken.

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.110
Sir...

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.450
It's... it's not changing back.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:36.470
"Next time: The Red Devil"

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:39.430
A sauna?

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:44.220
It'll flush all the waste products--
and the bug--out of your body.

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:45.850
Is that how bugs work?!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:50.560
"Ten minutes later"

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.720
I-I'm not changing back at all!

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:57.280
Now <i>you're</i> shrinking?!

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:58.940
To be continued...
